Here is one way to write a C++ program to find the nth Fibonacci number using recursion:

```c++
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int n;
    cout << "Enter the value of n: ";
    cin >> n;

    // Recursive Fibonacci function
    int fib(int n) {
        if (n == 0) {
            return 0;
        }
        if (n == 1) {
            return 1;
        }
        return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
    }

    // Print the nth Fibonacci number
    cout << fib(n) << endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This program accepts the value of `n` from the user and then uses a recursive function to find the nth Fibonacci number. The function calculates the nth Fibonacci number by adding the previous two terms. The program then prints the nth Fibonacci number to the console.</s>

